title One fold away from healthy is not healthy
prompt Autonomous lap after the fleet's account change. Baton, card, rota row 1 (air -- law and boundary, lap 4101 mod 5), reds first.
think Air row, and its sense is touch: you cannot touch a thing's middle, only where it ends. So read every boundary this lap meets by pressing on it and asking whether the hand passes through.
think The cold open answered guards_red=4 and TWO of the reds were one page -- equinox_e123 with pin_over_bound and declared_ceiling with over_declared_bound, both on construction/REDS.md at 41,153 of 40,960. Pressed the third instrument that reads that same page and the hand went straight through.
think reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh is titled "can the ledger still accept a row?" It printed pin_headroom=-193, pin_foldable_rows=7, rows_that_fit=0 -- and answered verdict=ok. Its verdict is reached by three shelf and recital conditions; capacity, the question it is named for, never touches it.
think Read its header before calling it wrong, because it argues the opposite on purpose: a full pin wants a person, raising a bound is Keaton's word, and a gate that reds on ordinary work is a gate somebody turns off. That argument is right -- for the pin it was written about.
think It is not about this cell, and the scan's own deadlock comment already says so one line down: "a full pin with a foldable row is one reds_fold.sh away from healthy." So the model was correct and only the report collapsed two states into one word.
obs THE THREE READS THAT MADE THIS A ROW RATHER THAN A TIDY. The bound was raised THAT MORNING at 20260906.022430, derived as 8 ships x 4,096 for the OPEN set; the OPEN set stood at 19,104 bytes, 58% of its allowance. The overflow was 18,153 bytes of already-foldable rows. So the pin reds while its live content sits at well under half -- the bound sizes what is OPEN and nothing measured what was merely undone.
obs THE COST, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. Walking git log for the day, 4 of 111 commit states carried the pin above its bound. In each, every ship's cold open read a red naming pin_over_bound and no remedy, while the one instrument that knows this ledger folds read ok.
obs I GATED THE CELL THAT IS BOTH AND LEFT THE ONE BESIDE IT ALONE. Over bound WITH a foldable row refuses by name, the fold command inside the refusal, because a lap repairs it in one command with no word from anyone. Over bound with NOTHING foldable stays reported, exactly as the header argues, since only a bound raise helps and that is Keaton's. Honoring an argument where it holds is different from deferring to it everywhere.
obs THE ELDER PENS SAT EXACTLY AT THE BOUND, NEVER OVER IT, which is why nothing already proven had to change: headroom==0 is not headroom<0. The witness kept its two legs and gained two, and the control went 31 cases to 39 -- the full 2x2 with every neighbouring cell shown free, since a refusal proven only in the failing direction cannot be told from a wall that always refuses.
obs MOST OF THIS LAP WAS RECOVERY, NOT AUTHORSHIP. stash_record red at unlanded=1 and named a whole signed lap parked in stash@{0} by my own round open: the jail_nesting fix, its session log, and a %510 fold. Landed it. Its %511 had been beaten by a peer's published %511, so it renumbered to %516 by the derived spine's own rule, across six citation sites in four files.
obs THE RECOVERED FIX WAS WORTH THE RECOVERY, AND I PROVED IT RATHER THAN TRUSTING IT. The elder probe handed bwrap /bin/true; this pier ships one entry in /bin. Measured here: elder spelling reads absent, new spelling reads present, and AGENT_JAIL_PART=enclosure runs all four legs GREEN -- host home invisible, Landlock fully enforced. Those legs had been skipped on this bench since 013116.
obs I NEARLY SHIPPED THE EXACT CITATION FAULT I BOOKED %502 FOR, TWO LAPS RUNNING. My shelf head cited %291 and linked the 276-280 shelf. Ran reds_citation before fixing it: GREEN. Staged the file and re-ran: it named the disagreement precisely. The guard reads git ls-files, so an unstaged file is outside every claim it makes -- the guard is right and the LAP was wrong about when to run it. Named on the card, unbooked.
obs THE CARD COST THIS LAP FIVE CONDENSATIONS AND IT IS NOT MY FINDING TO CLAIM. CHECKPOINTS.md already carries eleven cairns today, most of them this one page at its ceiling. I marked a twelfth, kept every live question Keaton has not answered word for word, and merged one question he is asked FOUR separate times on one card into the single place it is argued.
